'''''The History of the Britons''''' ({{langx|la|'''Historia Brittonum'''}}) is a purported history of early Britain written around 829-30 that survives in numerous [[recension]]s from after the 11th century. The ''Historia Brittonum'' is commonly attributed to [[Nennius]], as some recensions have a preface written in that name. Some experts have dismissed the Nennian preface as a late forgery<!-- ([[David Dumville|Dumville]], 1985) --> and argued that the work was actually an anonymous compilation.{{efn|name=Koch-anon|"Dumville has argued that the Nennian Prologue is a later forgery, so the work should therefore be treated as anonymous" {{Harv|Koch|2006|p=927}}}}{{efn|name=mackillop-DND|"Formerly ascribed to one Nennius, ''Historia'' is now seen, thanks to the work of David Dumville, to be a compilation..." {{harv|Mackillop|2004|loc=''Historia Brittonum''}}}}

